## Public documentation

`docs/src/docs/**` contains website pages, teaching references, examples and
topic navigation.

## Design scope

The public Design Scope route forms the sole authority for accepted, open and
excluded language boundaries:

- `docs/src/docs/design-scope/design-principles.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/design-scope/deferred-and-outside-scope.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/design-scope/excluded-language-families.mtf`

## Memory and lifetimes

The public Memory route covers source-facing memory behaviour:

- `docs/src/docs/memory/reference-semantics.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/reference-semantics-basic.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/copy-and-exclusive-access.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/copy-and-exclusive-access-basic.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/lifetimes-and-result-shapes.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/lifetimes-and-result-shapes-basic.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/declared-memory-groups.mtf`
- `docs/src/docs/memory/declared-memory-groups-basic.mtf`

The formal memory model, borrow validation, lifetime-region analysis and
backend lowering live under
`docs/src/docs/codebase/memory-management/**`.

